---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Annabel paints figures drawn from feminine archetypes and dreams, in acrylic on canvas, in Fort Lauderdale."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-site px-5 py-16 sm:px-12 sm:py-24">
		<h1 class="font-display text-[32px] font-light leading-[1.1] text-ink sm:text-[48px]">
			About
		</h1>

		<div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 sm:mt-16 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,360px)_1fr] sm:gap-16">
			<img
				class="aspect-[2/3] w-full object-cover"
				src="/annabel-about.jpg"
				width="1200"
				height="1800"
				alt="Annabel and her fiancé standing on a stone bridge beside a lake."
				loading="lazy"
				decoding="async"
			/>

			<div>
				<p class="max-w-prose text-charcoal">
					I paint people — contemporary, figurative work with an editorial, surrealist
					edge. I have painted since I was a child, and the images I keep returning to come
					from feminine archetypes and from what surfaces in my dreams. Acrylic on canvas,
					mostly. The figures feel familiar and slightly out of place: fragments of one
					interior life, made to fit into someone else&rsquo;s.
				</p>

				<p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-charcoal">
					For a long time it stayed private. I listed a few pieces on Facebook Marketplace
					almost as an experiment, and they moved fast — faster than I expected. That was
					the first real sign the work belonged to other people too, and it is what turned
					painting from a habit into a practice.
				</p>

				<p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-charcoal">
					I live and paint in Fort Lauderdale. Right now I am building toward a larger body
					of work and a first run of signed, limited-edition prints.
				</p>

				{/* [TODO] Ask Annabel: anything specific she is working toward this year —
				    a series, a show, a size she wants to grow into? Replace the second half
				    of the paragraph above with her own words. */}

				<p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-charcoal">
					My fianc&eacute; Preston handles the business side, and he is the one who kept
					telling me to share the work with the world.
				</p>

				<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
					<a class="btn" href="/originals">Shop originals</a>
					<a class="btn-secondary" href="/commissions">Request a commission</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
